A||||8||rogergarrison||3800 w/OD auto trans prob||||1||
Z||000000||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||08:17 PM||||im looking at buying a vehicle for its drive train. its a 94 GM FWD 3800, with the OD auto trans. My question is at cruising speed on freeway in OD, when i just barely touch gas it shakes and jerks, but if i accelerate quicker its OK. It doesnt seem to do it if I just leave it in D. The engine starts n runs perfectly and I just put in new plugs they were really burnt up bad. Didnt help ,Im thinking its in transmission, Lock up or something. I dont know anything about these new transmissions. Anyone with an idea to test before I have to pay someone to check it out. Im getting a really good buy and hate to pass, the engine is so good running and sounding except for this prob.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||01-10-2001||09:05 PM||||Weeeellll,<P>It sounds like something could be wrong with overdrive  since putting it in 3rd clears it up. The TCC still locks up in 3rd. This assumes you left it in 3rd long enough for the TCC to engage.<P>If you take it out and cruise at 50MPH in 3rd, steady speed, light throttle, you should be able to lightly press the brake pedal and the TCC will disengage. The RPM's will rise about 300-400 RPM. Release the brake and wait a few seconds and the TCC will re-engage. If that works, it's not the TCC. <P>While still cruising, slip it into 4th. It should shift and the TCC will engage. Do the brake tap test again.<P>When the jerking occurs, keep it jerking and light press the brake. Does the jerking stop?<P>I would check:<P>1. The vacuum modulator and lines going to it.<BR>2. TPS sensor. <BR>3. Check for codes.<P>Then take it to a shop. It's hard to troubleshoot like this.<P>Is the SES on? 94/95 won't flash codes. Needs a scanner.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||01-11-2001||08:09 AM||||My sister-in-law was having problems with her 94 Monte Carlo and it tuned out to be a leaking vacuum line. Cheap fix. Also, don't forget the obvious... how's the transmission fluid? Bright pink or brown. My neighbor's car (Crown Vic) was doing the same thing as yours. He had the transmission fluid and filter changed and the problem went away.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000003||elfiero||01-11-2001||10:04 AM||||These are the most likely  things:<BR>1.plug wires that have higher than normal<BR>resistance.<BR>2.a bad EGR valve-this is solinoid operated<BR>on all 3800's,and one of the three staged<BR>coils might have failed.<BR>3.low fuel pressure caused by dirt on the<BR>seat of the pressure regulator.when you step<BR>on the throttle harder,the vacuum drops,and<BR>the spring pushes harder on the seat in the<BR>fuel reg.<BR>4.A "chattering" clutch in the trans.Try<BR>adjusting the T-V cable <BR>this is just a few things to look at but<BR>I advise you to get all the bugs worked out<BR>before you pull it from the car.||||reg||6
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-11-2001||02:41 PM||||Ive got service records for it. just had the EGR valve replaced, and fluid looks and smells new, up too mark. Trans repr shops say they think its a motor prob, not trans. Im goint to let the dealer who has it check it out before i make him a final if any offer. Its in a minivan that im goin to use for a year or so, then put in a GT 40/Fiero kit Im going to build. Thanks for the info though guys.||||reg||1
Z||000005||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||01-13-2001||03:39 AM||||We had a similar shuddering problem with a 1988 Buick LeSabre T-Type (3800 V6/auto trans).  It turned out to be a spark plug wire in the end.  When you drove the car it seemed like an expensive transmission problem, but it wasn't<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||01-13-2001||11:54 AM||||I know what you are talking about (carbon tracking on a coil pack or plug. Seen it.) But he says it doesn't do it in D/3rd. I would expect it to do it in D and OD.<P>Also, 94's have linear EGR's, no digitals, and there won't be a TVS cable since it should be a 4T60E. Well, that's what we have here in California. Don't say it...<P>Let us know what you find. Always good information for the archives.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||01-13-2001||04:44 PM||||OK......dealer fixed it, bad coil pack. thanks for ur input guys.<P>since it only did it in overdrive, i figured for sure had to be in trans. Oh well dont you hate new cars.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||01-13-2001||08:12 PM||||Only did it in overdrive and it was the coil pack? Never seen that. When I cracked one, it would do it in any gear.<P>New information!<P>Terry||||reg||1
